  "summary": "Changing four sticky ends on one DNA-origami building block selects cubic diamond, hexagonal diamond, or ice 0.",
  "significance": "Changing the programmed vertex interactions of a single DNA-origami tetrahedron selects cubic diamond, hexagonal diamond, or ice 0, without redesigning the scaffold. The two diamonds differ only in stacking sequence, so the hexagonal crystal’s habit and ordered basal plane are not proof on their own; small-angle X-ray scattering resolves the stacking.",
